1
00:00:00,998 --> 00:00:05,002
For those of us who are worried about climate change,

2
00:00:05,002 --> 00:00:08,071
it's no doubt challenging times.

3
00:00:08,071 --> 00:00:11,408
It feels like the end of the light of the tunnel

4
00:00:11,408 --> 00:00:15,712
gets further as companies and governments pull back.

5
00:00:15,712 --> 00:00:19,283
And I get it. It's hard to feel motivated with headlines like these.

6
00:00:19,283 --> 00:00:22,219
But that is not the full story.

7
00:00:22,219 --> 00:00:24,621
In reality,

8
00:00:24,621 --> 00:00:29,192
a shift towards a climate solution-based economy is already underway.

9
00:00:29,192 --> 00:00:31,662
Not just because it protects the climate,

10
00:00:31,662 --> 00:00:35,132
but because it's becoming more profitable,

11
00:00:35,132 --> 00:00:39,369
more practical and more affordable.

12
00:00:39,369 --> 00:00:41,371
Despite all the setbacks,

13
00:00:41,371 --> 00:00:44,341
we will solve this problem.

14
00:00:44,341 --> 00:00:47,744
However, we have to be strategic.

15
00:00:47,744 --> 00:00:51,615
We cannot solve every climate problem at once.

16
00:00:51,615 --> 00:00:55,719
We have to identify the systems that can unlock many others.

17
00:00:55,719 --> 00:00:59,790
The places where one smart move can create ripple effects

18
00:00:59,790 --> 00:01:03,193
across the entire economy.

19
00:01:03,193 --> 00:01:06,730
One of the most strategic, most powerful,

20
00:01:06,730 --> 00:01:11,001
but also most overlooked of those systems is shipping.

21
00:01:11,001 --> 00:01:13,637
If shipping was a country,

22
00:01:13,637 --> 00:01:18,241
it would be the sixth largest greenhouse gas emitter in the world.

23
00:01:18,241 --> 00:01:20,944
Many of these ships aren't just powered by fossil fuels,

24
00:01:20,944 --> 00:01:24,648
they're built with fossil fuels, and they transport fossil fuels.

25
00:01:24,648 --> 00:01:29,620
Maritime shipping is a climate problem on three fronts.

26
00:01:29,620 --> 00:01:32,155
One, for the cargo it carries.

27
00:01:32,155 --> 00:01:36,293
Crude oil and gas account for roughly one third of maritime trade.

28
00:01:36,293 --> 00:01:40,797
Around half of natural gas is shipped in a liquefied form called LNG,

29
00:01:40,797 --> 00:01:43,734
and LNG trade has doubled during the past decade.

30
00:01:43,734 --> 00:01:47,404
Two, because of the fuel ships burn.

31
00:01:47,404 --> 00:01:49,673
Most ships still burn heavy fuel oils

32
00:01:49,673 --> 00:01:53,510
or increasingly, LNG, which releases carbon dioxide and methane,

33
00:01:53,510 --> 00:01:58,482
a dirty superpollutant that accelerates climate change and air pollution.

34
00:01:58,482 --> 00:02:02,219
Three, because of the steel ships are made of.

35
00:02:02,219 --> 00:02:05,689
Most steel is made using dirty coal.

36
00:02:05,689 --> 00:02:11,294
Steel production is responsible for another 8% of global emissions.

37
00:02:11,294 --> 00:02:14,464
So shipping is not a side issue in the climate crisis.

38
00:02:14,464 --> 00:02:18,335
It is one of the biggest hidden levers in the entire climate fight,

39
00:02:18,335 --> 00:02:20,504
a system if pulled the right way,

40
00:02:20,504 --> 00:02:23,540
which can unlock a faster energy transition.

41
00:02:23,540 --> 00:02:28,178
It's tempting to think of oceans as diffused and decentralized,

42
00:02:28,178 --> 00:02:30,380
but when it comes to ships,

43
00:02:30,380 --> 00:02:34,551
their supply chains converge in one place:

44
00:02:34,551 --> 00:02:35,819
East Asia.

45
00:02:35,819 --> 00:02:37,621
South Korea in particular

46
00:02:37,621 --> 00:02:40,991
dominates global shipbuilding, steel production for ships

47
00:02:40,991 --> 00:02:43,794
and the public finance behind them.

48
00:02:43,794 --> 00:02:46,763
And we are now at a critical moment,

49
00:02:46,763 --> 00:02:50,167
with Asia as a key leverage point.

50
00:02:50,167 --> 00:02:53,070
The world has experienced how volatile fossil fuels are

51
00:02:53,070 --> 00:02:55,038
with the war in Ukraine.

52
00:02:55,038 --> 00:02:59,576
Again, we are experiencing the same with the war in the Middle East.

53
00:02:59,576 --> 00:03:02,779
Right now, East Asian economies are making a decision.

54
00:03:02,779 --> 00:03:05,182
Do we keep funding fossil fuels

55
00:03:05,182 --> 00:03:07,617
or pivot towards offshore wind installation vessels,

56
00:03:07,617 --> 00:03:11,621
green ammonia tankers or ships made with clean steel?

57
00:03:11,621 --> 00:03:15,792
Because clean options don't scale just because they exist,

58
00:03:15,792 --> 00:03:18,829
they scale when policy, finance and regulation align

59
00:03:18,829 --> 00:03:21,698
to make clean attractive.

60
00:03:21,698 --> 00:03:24,367
My organization, Solutions for Our Climate,

61
00:03:24,367 --> 00:03:26,803
works to do just that.

62
00:03:26,803 --> 00:03:28,171
And we're no beginner here.

63
00:03:28,171 --> 00:03:29,906
We've done it before with coal.

64
00:03:29,906 --> 00:03:32,275
From behind-the-scenes international negotiations

65
00:03:32,275 --> 00:03:33,744
to grassroots communities,

66
00:03:33,744 --> 00:03:38,482
from courtrooms to hilarious videos portraying dismal climate facts,

67
00:03:38,482 --> 00:03:40,784
we know what message to put in front of who,

68
00:03:40,784 --> 00:03:43,053
how and when.

69
00:03:43,053 --> 00:03:46,189
Our work actually contributed to ending coal financing

70
00:03:46,189 --> 00:03:48,191
by the East Asian coal giants.

71
00:03:48,191 --> 00:03:51,862
(Applause)

72
00:03:51,862 --> 00:03:57,134
And now we're ready to take on shipping the same way.

73
00:03:57,134 --> 00:04:01,738
First, we expose emissions, policy gaps, financial risks.

74
00:04:01,738 --> 00:04:04,174
Take LNG transportation.

75
00:04:04,174 --> 00:04:08,011
Global LNG trade depends entirely on ships.

76
00:04:08,011 --> 00:04:10,747
Each LNG carrier ship

77
00:04:10,747 --> 00:04:12,916
costs 250 million dollars,

78
00:04:12,916 --> 00:04:17,454
takes three years to build and locks in decades of emissions.

79
00:04:17,454 --> 00:04:21,291
The system is surprisingly concentrated.

80
00:04:21,291 --> 00:04:25,095
70 percent of these ships are built in one country,

81
00:04:25,095 --> 00:04:26,363
South Korea.

82
00:04:26,363 --> 00:04:30,033
In 2022 alone, in one year, South Korean government banks

83
00:04:30,033 --> 00:04:34,404
provided more than 10 billion dollars of financing for these ships.

84
00:04:34,404 --> 00:04:40,377
The technologies around these ships are monopolized by a handful of companies.

85
00:04:40,377 --> 00:04:43,013
So this isn't just a business story.

86
00:04:43,013 --> 00:04:46,449
It's a political and financial choke point.

87
00:04:46,449 --> 00:04:50,120
Second, we redirect capital and governments

88
00:04:50,120 --> 00:04:53,490
away from fossil expansion.

89
00:04:53,490 --> 00:04:55,659
If we cut the financing of these ships,

90
00:04:55,659 --> 00:04:58,094
we will limit LNG expansion.

91
00:04:58,094 --> 00:04:59,362
Our aim is simple.

92
00:04:59,362 --> 00:05:02,999
Make LNG a no-investment zone.

93
00:05:02,999 --> 00:05:06,336
(Applause)

94
00:05:06,336 --> 00:05:10,941
We're asking private banks to end the financing of these ships.

95
00:05:10,941 --> 00:05:15,178
We're pushing Asian lenders to adopt exclusion policies.

96
00:05:15,178 --> 00:05:20,217
Third, we build markets, demands and rules for clean alternatives.

97
00:05:20,217 --> 00:05:24,554
The technology for clean steel or green shipping fuels is already here.

98
00:05:24,554 --> 00:05:29,292
What's missing is the supply chains and demand to meet it.

99
00:05:29,292 --> 00:05:33,363
Our push for finance, regulations and infrastructure will change this.

100
00:05:33,363 --> 00:05:36,666
That means building clean fuel supply chains,

101
00:05:36,666 --> 00:05:38,034
creating new demand

102
00:05:38,034 --> 00:05:41,004
through green shipping corridors between ports.

103
00:05:41,004 --> 00:05:45,041
Over time, renewable-rich regions will replace oil refineries

104
00:05:45,041 --> 00:05:47,277
as shipping fuel production hubs.

105
00:05:47,277 --> 00:05:50,881
We apply the same approach for clean steel.

106
00:05:50,881 --> 00:05:55,752
Green hydrogen will replace the role coal served in steelmaking.

107
00:05:55,752 --> 00:05:58,321
This isn't just aspirational.

108
00:05:58,321 --> 00:06:00,457
The work is already underway.

109
00:06:00,457 --> 00:06:03,260
We've already convinced four European banks

110
00:06:03,260 --> 00:06:07,163
to exit from a major LNG project in Mozambique.

111
00:06:07,163 --> 00:06:11,468
We've blocked new coal-based steel investments.

112
00:06:11,468 --> 00:06:15,171
We've secured financial support for hydrogen-based steel mills.

113
00:06:15,171 --> 00:06:18,708
We're doing the work and building the momentum.

114
00:06:18,708 --> 00:06:23,213
And now we will supercharge it through Navigate to Clean,

115
00:06:23,213 --> 00:06:27,617
a new initiative to clean up maritime shipping.

116
00:06:27,617 --> 00:06:32,289
With the generous support of the community of Audacious donors,

117
00:06:32,289 --> 00:06:34,291
we will turn shipping

118
00:06:34,291 --> 00:06:37,027
from a conduit of dirty trade

119
00:06:37,027 --> 00:06:39,429
to a driver of clean trade.

120
00:06:39,429 --> 00:06:45,502
We are a team of marketers, diplomats, lawyers, shipping experts.

121
00:06:45,502 --> 00:06:48,004
We're a regional organization with global reach.

122
00:06:48,004 --> 00:06:50,573
We know the system and how to move it.

123
00:06:50,573 --> 00:06:55,211
We've done it with coal and we can do it with shipping.

124
00:06:55,211 --> 00:06:59,316
It is difficult times, yes, but with the right strategy and leverage,

125
00:06:59,316 --> 00:07:05,255
we can eliminate up to 2.2 gigatons of emissions per year by 2032.

126
00:07:05,255 --> 00:07:08,925
That's almost one year of emissions of the entire European Union.

127
00:07:08,925 --> 00:07:14,531
(Applause)

128
00:07:14,531 --> 00:07:16,299
This is not a marginal fix.

129
00:07:16,299 --> 00:07:19,502
This is not tinkering at the edges.

130
00:07:19,502 --> 00:07:23,907
This is what it looks like to move a hidden engine of the global economy

131
00:07:23,907 --> 00:07:26,209
and the climate movement with it.

132
00:07:26,209 --> 00:07:29,746
We're playing chess, not checkers, and we're here to win.

133
00:07:29,746 --> 00:07:31,247
Thank you.

134
00:07:31,247 --> 00:07:35,247
(Applause)
